    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0062" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg30"/>

                <head>19. Telegram From the Secretary of State to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d19-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-05-06T23:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1958—11
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Dulte 10. Re Tedul 8 and Tosec 29.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d19-f2"/> After
                    conferring with Mr. Lloyd and Mr.
                        Laloy we agree with basic policy decision to support
                        Chamoun on basis of paragraph 3 of
                    joint appreciation<anchor n="3" xml:id="d19-f3"/> of British, French and
                    American Ambassadors.</p>
                <pb facs="0063" n="31" xml:id="pg31"/>
                <p>Secretary leaves to Department and Embassy the implementing of this basic
                    decision in accord with British and French but suggests that if we do back
                        Chamoun we should do so wholeheartedly
                    and possibly Tedul 8 might be somewhat depressing for Chamoun.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 783A.00/5–658. Top Secret; Niact.
                    Also sent to Beirut.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f2" n="2" xml:id="d19-f2-content">
                <p>Tosec 29 to Copenhagen, May 5, repeated to the Secretary the texts of telegrams
                    3673 and 3674 from Beirut. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.,</hi> Conference
                    Files: Lot 63 D 123, CF 1505) Telegram 3674 is <ref target="#d18"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">supra</hi></ref>, and telegram 3673 is summarized in
                        <ref target="#d18-f2">footnote 2, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi></ref>.
                    Tedul 8 to Copenhagen, May 5, from Herter to Dulles, also
                    sent to Beirut as telegram 4173, suggested that, in view of the short time
                    remaining before McClintock’s May 7
                    meeting with Chamoun, Dulles should coordinate a U.S.–U.K.–French
                    position on the impending Lebanese presidential election with Selwyn Lloyd and the French representative at
                    the NATO meeting in Copenhagen. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">3½ lines of text not declassified</hi>] (Department of
                    State, Central Files, 783A.11/5–558; included in <ref
                        target="frus1958-60v11mSupp">the microfiche supplement</ref>)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f3" n="3" xml:id="d19-f3-content">
                <p>Transmitted in telegram 3674, <ref target="#d18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
